# Project Instructions

> Built with the DoNotDev framework. Guardrails are hook-enforced - quality is automatic.

## How to work with you

Just tell me what you want. "I need a dashboard page" or "add a contact form" - I'll handle the rest.

I use the DoNotDev framework's component library which covers 99% of what apps need. I verify every component via MCP before using it, so props and APIs are always correct.

## What happens behind the scenes (you don't need to know this)

Quality hooks run automatically on every change I make. They catch mistakes before they reach you. If something is wrong, I fix it silently and move on.

## What you'll see

- I build features incrementally, committing at milestones
- I'll ask clarifying questions if your request is ambiguous
- When done, I'll show you what was built and how to verify it
- `dndev tc` verifies type safety, `dndev dev` runs the app locally

## Adding dependencies

Need a library the framework doesn't cover? Just ask - I can add packages with `bun add`.

## Conventions I follow

- All text is translatable (i18n-ready from day one)
- Framework components for UI (no raw HTML, no custom CSS)
- Clean, simple code a junior developer can read
- Typecheck passes before any work is considered complete

Read `AI.md` for project-specific instructions.
